 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Asking permission with care",
     "texto": [
      "You already know **¿Puedo…?** and **¿Se puede…?**. There are other, kinder ways:\n\n- **¿Te importa si** abro la ventana? (with **si**, indicative)\n- **¿Te importa que** abra la ventana? (with **que**, subjunctive)\n- **¿Te molesta que** abra la ventana?\n- **¿Me dejas** usar tu cargador?\n\nWith **¿te importa…?** the answer is reversed: **no, en absoluto** means you may; **sí, me importa** means you may not.\n\nTo give permission with a condition: **Vale, pero** devuélvemelo antes de las cinco. To refuse tactfully: **Me temo que no**.\n\nSigns say: **Está prohibido** fumar. **No está permitido** entrar con perros. **Se prohíbe** el paso."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Si, que and the subjunctive",
     "texto": [
      "The question changes with the word that follows:\n\n- **¿Te importa si** + indicative? *¿Te importa si me siento aquí?*\n- **¿Te importa que** + subjunctive? *¿Te importa que me siente aquí?*\n- **¿Te molesta que** + subjunctive? *¿Te molesta que abra la ventana?*\n\nIn rules, the verb that follows depends on the subject:\n\n- If there is no other subject, use the **infinitive**: *Está prohibido fumar.*\n- If there is another subject, use **que** and the **subjunctive**: *Está prohibido que los niños entren solos.*\n\nRespecting the rule avoids a fine."
     ],
